---
const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy – Blind Pixels Studio";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Privacy policy for Blind Pixels Studio, explaining what information is collected and how it is used."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="page">
    <main class="layout" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Blind Pixels Studio</a>

      <header class="header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
        <h1 id="privacy-heading">How Blind Pixels Studio handles your data</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Blind Pixels Studio is a small, independent studio that builds accessibility-first
          tools and experiments. This page explains what limited information we collect and how
          we use it.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Blind Pixels Studio is an independent project run by a solo developer. The website and
          tools are operated on a best-effort basis. If you have any questions about this policy,
          you can reach out via the contact form on this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We aim to collect as little personal information as possible.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact form:</strong> When you use the contact form, we collect the name,
            email address, subject, and message that you provide so we can read and respond to
            your inquiry.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Emails and replies:</strong> If you reply to any emails we send, those
            responses will be stored in our email provider.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>App usage:</strong> Individual apps may collect minimal information needed
            for them to function (for example, settings or preferences). When this happens, it is
            limited to that app and is not sold or shared for advertising.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not intentionally collect sensitive personal information. Please avoid sending
          sensitive data (such as passwords, financial information, or health information) through
          the contact form.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The Blind Pixels Studio website is designed to be simple and low-tracking. At this
          time, we do not use third-party analytics scripts (such as Google Analytics) or ad
          trackers on this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our hosting provider may collect basic technical logs (for example, IP address and
          request metadata) in order to operate the service and keep it secure.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To read and respond to messages you send through the contact form.</li>
          <li>To maintain and improve the website and apps.</li>
          <li>To troubleshoot issues or investigate abuse or spam.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information or share it with third
          parties for advertising purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Where your data is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Contact form submissions are delivered via email using a third-party email service
          provider (currently Resend). That provider processes the information you submit in order
          to deliver the email to us. Your message and email address may also be stored in our
          email inbox for as long as reasonably necessary to handle your inquiry.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>How long we keep your information</h2>
        <p>
          We keep emails and contact form messages for as long as they are useful for support or
          record-keeping, or until you reasonably ask us to delete them, and we are able to do so.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>You can choose not to use the contact form or provide personal information.</li>
          <li>
            You can request that we delete previous email conversations, where practicable, by
            contacting us again through the form.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Children&apos;s privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Blind Pixels Studio is not directed toward children under 13, and we do not knowingly
          collect personal information from children. If you believe that a child has provided us
          with personal information, please contact us so we can take appropriate steps.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this privacy policy from time to time as the website or apps evolve. When
          we do, we will update the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date on this page. Your continued use of
          the site after changes are posted means you accept those changes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this policy or how your information is handled, please
          reach out through the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer">
        <p>Last updated: November 17, 2025</p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>

  <style lang="css">
    body.page {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: "Inter", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at top left, #111827 0%, #020617 60%);
      color: #f9fafb;
    }

    .layout {
      width: min(900px, 100% - 3rem);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem;
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      color: #bfdbfe;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .back-link:hover,
    .back-link:focus {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .header {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      color: #a5b4fc;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
      font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    }

    .lede {
      margin: 0;
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
      color: rgba(226, 232, 255, 0.9);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 46rem;
    }

    .section {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding-top: 1.25rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 209, 0.25);
    }

    .section h2 {
      margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
      font-size: 1.2rem;
    }

    .section p {
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
      color: rgba(209, 213, 219, 0.98);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .section ul {
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
      padding-left: 1.1rem;
      color: rgba(209, 213, 219, 0.98);
    }

    .section li {
      margin: 0.25rem 0;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .section a {
      color: #93c5fd;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .section a:hover,
    .section a:focus {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .footer {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 209, 0.25);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.95);
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .layout {
        width: min(100%, 100% - 2.5rem);
        padding: 3rem 0 4.5rem;
      }

      .section {
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</html>
